===============================================================================

  RailsLti has been installed! Next steps:

  1. Run the migration:
       rails db:migrate

  2. Mount the engine in config/routes.rb (already added):
       mount RailsLti::Engine => "/lti"

  3. Configure the engine in config/initializers/rails_lti.rb.
     At minimum, set your tool URL and private key:

       RailsLti.configure do |config|
         config.tool_url   = "https://mytool.example.com"
         config.private_key = Rails.application.credentials.lti_private_key
       end

  4. Register your tool with an LTI 1.3 platform:
     - Manually: create a RailsLti::Platform and RailsLti::Deployment record.
     - Automatically: direct the platform admin to GET /lti/registration
       with the openid_configuration URL.

  5. See the README for full usage documentation.

===============================================================================
